\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces PCF-CTF framework: Three independent components (origin production O$_i$ from features, distance decay f(d) from aggregate data, destination attraction A$_j$ from features) are evaluated via a 25-city training and 25-city held-out zero-shot validation framework, where the model is evaluated on the 25 held-out cities without target-city OD data. Key innovation: SHAP-based feature stability selection identifies 22 transferable features from 30 open-data candidates (OSM + WorldPop + Meta). Note: The source cities shown in the diagram (e.g., New York, Chicago, Houston) are illustrative examples only, as the full list of 25 source and 25 held-out target cities is selected dynamically across the 50-city pool.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:graphical_abstract}{{1}{2}{PCF-CTF framework: Three independent components (origin production O$_i$ from features, distance decay f(d) from aggregate data, destination attraction A$_j$ from features) are evaluated via a 25-city training and 25-city held-out zero-shot validation framework, where the model is evaluated on the 25 held-out cities without target-city OD data. Key innovation: SHAP-based feature stability selection identifies 22 transferable features from 30 open-data candidates (OSM + WorldPop + Meta). Note: The source cities shown in the diagram (e.g., New York, Chicago, Houston) are illustrative examples only, as the full list of 25 source and 25 held-out target cities is selected dynamically across the 50-city pool}{figure.1}{}}
