\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Conceptual comparison of the existing locally dependent modeling paradigm versus our zero-shot transferable paradigm. Under the existing paradigm, models require target-city OD observations to retrain or calibrate parameters. In our paradigm, we learn transferable mechanisms ($O_i, f(d), A_j$) using globally available open data features in source City A and transfer them directly to City B without target-city OD data.}}{4}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:conceptual_framework}{{2}{4}{Conceptual comparison of the existing locally dependent modeling paradigm versus our zero-shot transferable paradigm. Under the existing paradigm, models require target-city OD observations to retrain or calibrate parameters. In our paradigm, we learn transferable mechanisms ($O_i, f(d), A_j$) using globally available open data features in source City A and transfer them directly to City B without target-city OD data}{figure.2}{}}
